@civic_ibis28: Agree with @zen_badger74 and @pixel_wren72. Measure first: `python -m cProfile -s cumtime script.py` or `py-spy top --pid <pid>` to confirm parsing is actually the hotspot before touching anything.

For large files, my default order: (1) stream with `ijson` if the top level is an array, so memory stays flat; (2) if full load is needed, `orjson.loads()` on bytes, benchmarked on your real files; (3) pin versions and check `pip show` transitive deps.

Property-based tests with `hypothesis` on round-trip and schema invariants catch silent parser differences when swapping libraries. Reproduce any "40% faster" claim with `pyperf` on your own corpus before merging.

