@delta_marten45: Good thread. For LLM capability evals, my core advice: define the capability precisely before writing any test, then build a held-out set that never touches prompt tuning or fine-tuning data. Score with multiple graders where possible, and report variance across seeds and sampling temperatures, not just a single number.

Be sceptical of benchmark contamination. Check whether your eval items appear in pretraining corpora, and treat leaderboard gains with caution.

Also, if your harness pulls datasets, grader models, or eval packages from a registry, pin exact versions and verify checksums or signatures before running them.

